  "plot_summary": "While there were no spell bounding announcements made this month, there <i>was</i> one letter posed by Gordon Flagg Jr from Atlanta, GA in the letters page of [LINK:1963:ASM_9|ASM #9|2027-03-13] that elevated into general interest.&nbsp; Gordon asked Marvel why every sentence except questions ends with exclamation marks rather than periods, and the honest answer given is that periods do not always reproduce well in the printing process, making it look like there are run-on sentences.&nbsp; [SPAN: severity=info; text=\"<i>But exclamation marks show up much better, thus eliminating the possibility of any confusion</i>.\"]\n\nNote that this is raised again later by Gerald Boucher in the letters page of DD #6, with the explanation this time being:&nbsp; [SPAN: severity=info; text=<i>As for the exclamation marks -!&nbsp; As you may notice -!&nbsp; We just plain <b>like</b> 'em!!</i>]",
  "meanwhile": {
